From: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:03:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] sched/cpufreq_schedutil: cap IO wait boost to prevent thermal overheating on fanless gateways

================================================================================
MAXNET High-Performance Kernel Engine & Hardware Architecture Optimization
Engineered & Developed by Mahendra Mali (Max) for MAXNET Router OS
Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
================================================================================

Cap IO wait boost to 50% capacity to prevent fanless thermal saturation on quad Cortex-A73.

Signed-off-by: Mahendra Mali (Max) <max@maxnet.lan>
---
--- a/kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/cpufreq_schedutil.c
@@ -307,8 +307,13 @@
 
 	/* Double the boost at each request */
 	if (sg_cpu->iowait_boost) {
+		/* MAXNET Thermal Optimization by Mahendra Mali (Max):
+		 * Cap IO wait boost to 50% capacity to prevent fanless thermal runaway (61C+).
+		 * Heavy network traffic still scales to max frequency via standard util tracking.
+		 * Copyright (c) 2026 Mahendra Mali - Max. All Rights Reserved.
+		 */
 		sg_cpu->iowait_boost =
-			min_t(unsigned int, sg_cpu->iowait_boost << 1, SCHED_CAPACITY_SCALE);
+			min_t(unsigned int, sg_cpu->iowait_boost << 1, SCHED_CAPACITY_SCALE >> 1);
 		return;
 	}
 
